+
+## Global Large text in the Team arena
+
+The shared text-size preference now reaches the Team painter alongside the font family and effects preference in one display snapshot. Standard retains the preceding drawing sizes. Large multiplies each resolved CSS font size by 4/3 after its existing clamp: 12-pixel role labels and downed plus become 16 pixels, 14-pixel pilot numerals become 18⅔ pixels, and the 18-pixel ceiling becomes 24. Omitting the painter option selects Standard; unsupported explicit values fail the existing text-size validation contract.
+
+Text-owned geometry grows with those glyphs. Large pilot circle/diamond badges are 27/32 CSS pixels; the downed-plus backing is 14×22. Caption padding, spacing from actor bodies and badge gaps scale together. These are cosmetic dimensions: actor frames, contact radii, cutting heads, terrain and simulation remain unchanged. Settings edits keep the accepted picture and current attempt, and closing Settings still requires explicit Resume.
+
+Large-only placement reserves complete plates in descending area, then draws them in their original cue order. If the ordinary candidate positions all overlap earlier plates, a bounded obstacle-edge sweep looks for free space. True player heads and active enemy contacts are hard exclusions. This does not preserve the entire painter order: Large captions appear after the intervening trails and warnings, with the final player cutting heads still drawn above them. Standard keeps its original immediate placement and command path.
+
+Maintenance prompt: “Change Team arena typography through the shared Standard/Large preference. Keep Standard canvas commands unchanged, then compare both font families and both arenas at the same CSS width. Check every required role glyph, both numbered badges and the downed marker; enlarge complete backings, preserve head clearance and board bounds, and retain the accepted picture and paused state. Include imported strongholds and report label overlaps and role association separately from glyph counts. Return exact source evidence and native layout checks.”
+
+The placement heuristic does not guarantee disjoint labels for every dense import. A modeled eight-stronghold case retains all 29 glyphs with no plate overlap at 362 CSS pixels after batching, but 320/304/292-pixel variants still add overlaps compared with Standard. These are recorded failures of modeled plate geometry; actual glyph obstruction and role association require native inspection with the shipped fonts. The global candidate remains unaccepted while this readability concern is unresolved. Neither board width nor imported-map complexity is silently restricted to make this check pass. A complete set of emitted labels alone is not readable layout evidence. Qualify crowding, actual font metrics, light/dark artwork, the combined HUD/board/touch layout, Large/Plain, zoom and physical devices separately. The local source proposal does not close P05, Team presentation parity or public-release qualification.
